## Solution Idea

For each cell record which of its 4 side‑midpoints are touched. Introduce edge variables

* `h[i][j]` = 1 iff the midpoint of the edge between (i,j) and (i,j+1 mod W) is touched,
* `v[i][j]` = 1 iff the midpoint of the edge between (i,j) and (i+1 mod H,j) is touched.

Then cell (i,j) has left = `h[i][j-1]`, right = `h[i][j]`, top = `v[i-1][j]`, bottom = `v[i][j]`, and:

* **Kind A** (two adjacent sides): exactly one of left/right and exactly one of top/bottom →
 `h[i][j-1] ⊕ h[i][j] = 1`, `v[i-1][j] ⊕ v[i][j] = 1`.
* **Kind B** (two opposite sides): `h[i][j-1] = h[i][j]`, `v[i-1][j] = v[i][j]`, and additionally `h[i][j] ≠ v[i][j]` (horizontal bar ⇒ h=1,v=0; vertical bar ⇒ h=0,v=1).

Every valid assignment of the edge variables corresponds to exactly one tile orientation per cell, so we just count assignments.

Along a row the recurrence `h[i][j] = h[i][j-1] ⊕ [S_ij = A]` must close up cyclically ⇒ **each row must contain an even number of A**; then `h[i][j] = a_i ⊕ P_{i,j}` with a free bit `a_i` and prefix xor `P_{i,j}`. Symmetrically **each column must contain an even number of A**, and `v[i][j] = b_j ⊕ Q_{i,j}`.

The remaining constraints come only from B cells:

```
a_i ⊕ b_j = 1 ⊕ P_{i,j} ⊕ Q_{i,j}
```

This is a parity (weighted) union–find system on `H+W` variables. If consistent, the answer is `2^(#components)`, otherwise `0`. (Parity failures of a row/column also give 0.)

Sample check: case 1 gives one component → 2 ✓, case 2 has an odd row → 0 ✓, case 3 gives one component → 2 ✓.

Complexity: `O(HW·α)` per test, total `O(10^6 α)`.

